From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: a fair count of how live graphics keys meet the shader set's records, with the render-state fields of near misses (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY), log only, off by default

What: the shader set's audit counts a hit only when a kept record carrying the set's flag
was drawn, so a house the console's own records already served showed "0 of 430" whatever the
set held (our notes (a)). With EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY=1 (and EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET=1) every
graphics pipeline made at runtime is sampled after the kept-translation check, and once the set's
catalogue is ready it is sorted into one bucket: mesh (task/mesh stage: the set has no mesh
records, so never a hit), hit_fair (the key is in the set and a set record was drawn), hit_own
(an own record was drawn; how many of those keys the set also holds), exact_refused (in the set
and in the store, refused by the answer check or remembered as not keepable), exact_not_prepared
(in the set, not prepared yet), exact_no_store, near (same six programs, other render state; the
closest record's differing FixedPipelineState fields are counted and, for the first 200, named),
no_record (split by whether all its programs are in the set).

The catalogue keeps no keys (a review: 1,056 B a key, about 114 MiB on the console that dies
of memory): per record a sorted key hash, the program tuple's hash and one 16-bit digest per
FixedPipelineState field (19 fields, a static_assert checks they cover the struct): about 64 B a
record, about 7 MiB for 113,054 records; the log line gives the real size. It is read on the set's
thread after the live-first pass, with keys only (no environments built). Near-miss candidates
per tuple are capped (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY_NEAR, 64), named lines too
(EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY_LINES, 200). Samples wait (at most 4,096; more are counted as dropped)
until the catalogue is ready; each keeps only the key hash, the six program hashes and the 19
field digests (about 104 B, about 416 KiB at the cap), and when no catalogue will come (the read
failed, or the set has no records) sampling stops and the waiting samples are let go. Totals print with the set's audit line every 60 s, not only at
shutdown (review S1-B (a): a start that dies at the door left nothing).

Log: "EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY: on ..." once; "EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY: catalogue of N records (K
KiB) in S s ..."; "EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY near live=<hash> states_in_set=N closest differs in
<fields>"; "EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_WHY totals: asked= resolved= waiting= dropped= mesh= hit_fair=
hit_own= (in set) hit_set_unlisted= exact_refused= exact_not_prepared= exact_no_store= near=
(capped) no_record= (programs all in set, some not) hit_old= catalogue= valid=; near fields:".
Off: one switch read in the constructor, one bool test per new graphics pipeline and in
CreateKeptGraphicsPipeline's refusal path; nothing read, allocated or logged. It changes nothing that is built or drawn.

Credits: the fair-count idea and the first draft (S1a): our own draft, reviewed twice; the
shader set and canonical keys build on Fritchii v5.5 (Frizti) and Vampinity's 0480/0501-0529.
